# Shot Prediction Neural Network

Build a NN to predict shot success probability using positional tracking data, reproducing the baseline 16 features from prior work and extending with novel spatial, physics-based, and player archetype features.

## What You Already Have (in [game.py](file:///c:/Users/juanm/Documents/KUL_MAI/TFM/TFM-KUL-Juan/game.py))

| Capability | Method | What it gives us |
|---|---|---|
| Player positions per frame | [_get_moment_details()](file:///c:/Users/juanm/Documents/KUL_MAI/TFM/TFM-KUL-Juan/game.py#627-691) | x, y for all 10 players + ball |
| Shot detection | [_get_player_actions()](file:///c:/Users/juanm/Documents/KUL_MAI/TFM/TFM-KUL-Juan/game.py#605-626) | Frame times for made/missed FGs |
| Velocity & acceleration | [get_player_physics()](file:///c:/Users/juanm/Documents/KUL_MAI/TFM/TFM-KUL-Juan/game.py#1233-1286) | [vx, vy] and [ax, ay] per player |
| Time-to-reach | [_time_to_reach()](file:///c:/Users/juanm/Documents/KUL_MAI/TFM/TFM-KUL-Juan/game.py#1001-1069) | Physics-based time for player to reach a point |
| Voronoi areas | [get_voronoi_areas()](file:///c:/Users/juanm/Documents/KUL_MAI/TFM/TFM-KUL-Juan/game.py#944-1000) | Court area controlled by each team |
| Space control | [get_space_control()](file:///c:/Users/juanm/Documents/KUL_MAI/TFM/TFM-KUL-Juan/game.py#1070-1170) | Heatmap of delta-distance or delta-time |
| Convex hull | [get_spacing_area()](file:///c:/Users/juanm/Documents/KUL_MAI/TFM/TFM-KUL-Juan/game.py#922-943) | Team spacing area |
| Offensive team | [get_offensive_team()](file:///c:/Users/juanm/Documents/KUL_MAI/TFM/TFM-KUL-Juan/game.py#1176-1211) | Which team has the ball |
| Shot clock | `moments['shot_clock']` | Time remaining |

## Proposed Changes

### Phase 1: Player Archetype Clustering

#### [NEW] [player_archetypes.py](file:///c:/Users/juanm/Documents/KUL_MAI/TFM/TFM-KUL-Juan/player_archetypes.py)

Use K-means to bin players into archetype categories, replacing raw player IDs (which would overfit).

**Shooter clustering metrics** (aggregated per-player across games):

| Metric | Source | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| FG% by zone (paint/mid/3pt) | pbp + positions | Core shooting ability profile |
| Avg shot distance | positions at shot time | Range preference |
| Catch-and-shoot % | velocity at shot time | Ball-handler vs spot-up |
| Shot volume (attempts/min) | pbp | High-volume vs selective |
| Avg shooter speed at shot | [get_player_physics()](file:///c:/Users/juanm/Documents/KUL_MAI/TFM/TFM-KUL-Juan/game.py#1233-1286) | Stationary vs off-movement |

**Defender clustering metrics**:

| Metric | Source | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| Avg contest distance | positions when opponent shoots | Close-out ability |
| Avg time-to-contest | [_time_to_reach()](file:///c:/Users/juanm/Documents/KUL_MAI/TFM/TFM-KUL-Juan/game.py#1001-1069) | Recovery speed |
| Avg speed while defending | [get_player_physics()](file:///c:/Users/juanm/Documents/KUL_MAI/TFM/TFM-KUL-Juan/game.py#1233-1286) | Activity level |
| Shots defended per min | pbp + proximity | Defensive engagement |

**Validation approach for K:**
1. **Elbow method**: Plot inertia vs K (K=2..10), look for diminishing returns
2. **Silhouette score**: Maximize average silhouette across clusters
3. **Downstream validation**: Compare model accuracy across K values — the K that maximizes shot prediction AUC wins

> [!NOTE]
> Expected outcome: ~3-5 shooter types (e.g., "elite volume", "catch-and-shoot specialist", "paint scorer", "selective midrange") and ~3-4 defender types (e.g., "rim protector", "perimeter lockdown", "help defender").

---

### Phase 2: Feature Extraction

#### [NEW] [shot_features.py](file:///c:/Users/juanm/Documents/KUL_MAI/TFM/TFM-KUL-Juan/shot_features.py)

For each shot attempt: identify shooter from pbp, find frame, compute features.

**Baseline 16 features** (reproducing prior work):

| # | Feature | Computation |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | [dist](file:///c:/Users/juanm/Documents/KUL_MAI/TFM/TFM-KUL-Juan/game.py#1171-1176) | Euclidean distance shooter → nearest basket |
| 2 | `x` | Shooter x-coordinate |
| 3 | `y` | Shooter y-coordinate |
| 4 | `shot_angle` | Angle of shot vector w.r.t. court center line |
| 5 | `closest_def_dist` | Min distance shooter → any defender |
| 6 | `closest_def_angle` | Closest defender angle w.r.t. shooter→basket |
| 7 | `num_close_defs` | Defenders within 4 feet |
| 8 | `shot_clock` | From `moments.shot_clock` |
| 9-10 | `shooter_par/perp_vel` | Shooter velocity decomposed into parallel/perpendicular to shot vector |
| 11-12 | `def_par/perp_vel` | Same for closest defender |
| 13-14 | `shooter_par/perp_acc` | Shooter acceleration decomposed |
| 15-16 | `def_par/perp_acc` | Same for closest defender |

**Novel features** (your improvements):

| # | Feature | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| 17 | `time_to_contest` | Physics-based δ_time from Lyon 3pt (proven > δ_space) |
| 18 | `offense_convex_hull` | Team spacing — correlated with ball movement quality |
| 19 | `defense_convex_hull` | How spread the defense is |
| 20 | `space_control_at_shot` | Delta-time control value at shooter position |
| 21 | `is_catch_and_shoot` | Binary: different biomechanics & accuracy profiles |
| 22 | `2nd_closest_def_dist` | Help defense pressure |
| 23 | `2nd_closest_def_time` | Help defense time-to-reach |
| 24 | `is_3_pointer` | Hard reward boundary (2pt vs 3pt) |
| 25 | `shooter_archetype` | K-means cluster ID (one-hot encoded) |
| 26 | `defender_archetype` | K-means cluster ID for closest defender (one-hot encoded) |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Target variable**: `made_shot` (binary) from pbp (`EVENTMSGTYPE == 1` → made, `== 2` → missed).

---

### Phase 3: Neural Network

#### [NEW] [shot_model.py](file:///c:/Users/juanm/Documents/KUL_MAI/TFM/TFM-KUL-Juan/shot_model.py)

Architecture inspired by EPV MIT (4 layers, 512 neurons), adapted:

```
Input (continuous features + one-hot archetypes)
→ BatchNorm
→ Dense(256) + ReLU + Dropout(0.3)
→ Dense(256) + ReLU + Dropout(0.3)  
→ Dense(128) + ReLU + Dropout(0.2)
→ Dense(64) + ReLU + Dropout(0.2)
→ Dense(1) + Sigmoid
```

- **Loss**: Binary cross-entropy  
- **Optimizer**: Adam + learning rate scheduling  
- **Evaluation**: Accuracy, AUC-ROC, calibration plot  
- **Split**: 70/15/15 train/val/test  
- **Framework**: PyTorch

> [!NOTE]
> Baseline target: 63% accuracy (prior work). Goal: beat this with novel features + archetypes.

## Configuration

- **Data scope**: Single game — GSW @ DEN (01.13.2016)
- **Conda environment**: `mecasport`
- **Total features**: 16 baseline + 10 novel = 26 (+ one-hot expansion for archetypes)

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Sanity-check features on 1 shot (manual distance calculation)
- No NaN leaks in feature matrix
- Model trains without errors

### Manual Verification
- Accuracy vs 63% baseline
- Feature importance / SHAP analysis — do novel features (time_to_contest, archetypes) actually help?
- Calibration plot: predicted probabilities ≈ actual make rates
- Ablation study: model with/without archetypes, with/without physics features
